.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead dep add" 1  "bead dep add " 
.SH NAME
bead dep add \- Add a dependency edge
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead dep add\fR [\fB\-\-kind\fR] [\fB\-\-condition\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIBLOCKED\fR> <\fIBLOCKER\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a dependency relationship between two issues.
.PP
Creates a directional dependency edge from blocked issue to blocker issue.
The \*(Aqblocks\*(Aq kind affects readiness; \*(Aqrelates_to\*(Aq and \*(Aqverifies\*(Aq do not affect
readiness but allow tracking related work.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead dep add BLOCKED BLOCKER                       # Add blocks dependency
  bead dep add task\-1 task\-2 \-\-kind blocks            # Explicit blocks
  bead dep add feature\-a bug\-fix \-\-kind relates_to     # Non\-blocking relationship
  bead dep add impl\-x check\-y \-\-kind verifies          # check\-y checks impl\-x\*(Aqs work
.PP
DEPENDENCY KINDS:
  \- blocks: BLOCKED is blocked until BLOCKER is closed (affects readiness)
  \- relates_to: Related issues without blocking semantics (cycles allowed)
  \- verifies: BLOCKER checks the work BLOCKED performs (never affects readiness)
.PP
CYCLE DETECTION:
  \*(Aqblocks\*(Aq dependencies cannot create cycles.
  Adding an edge that creates a directed cycle will fail with exit code 4.
  \*(Aqrelates_to\*(Aq and \*(Aqverifies\*(Aq edges can form cycles (no restriction).
.PP
INVERTED VERIFICATION GATES:
  A `blocks` edge whose blocker also `verifies` the blocked issue orders the
  check before the work it checks, which no execution can satisfy. `bead
  doctor \-\-scope dependencies` reports each such pair as an advisory warning;
  the edges stay legal because a deliberate baseline\-first gate looks
  identical. The relationship is never inferred from issue titles.
.PP
READINESS IMPACT:
  Only \*(Aqblocks\*(Aq dependencies affect ready frontier:
  \- Issue is ready when: open, unassigned, not manually blocked, no unfinished blockers
  \- Blocker is unfinished when: not in closed state
  \- Finishing a blocker may expose dependent issues to ready frontier
.PP
IDEMPOTENCY:
  Adding an existing dependency succeeds without error.
  Self\-edges (blocked == blocker) are rejected (exit code 4).
.PP
ORIENTATION:
  Syntax is: bead dep add <BLOCKED> <BLOCKER>
  BLOCKED depends on BLOCKER completing first
  BLOCKER must finish before BLOCKED can be ready
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI<KIND>\fR [default: blocks]
Dependency kind: blocks, relates_to, or verifies (default: blocks)
.TP
\fB\-\-condition\fR \fI<CONDITION>\fR
Conditional dependency expression as JSON (optional)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Dry run: show what would happen without making changes
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIBLOCKED\fR>
Blocked issue ID
.TP
<\fIBLOCKER\fR>
Blocker issue ID
